236: radial normalization on the link. The unrestricted
237: four-weight common-link identity then gives the
238: literal \(T(y,q_H)=(q_H^{-1}yq_H,q_H)\) extension,
239: with the same fixed complex-normal reset as K62.
240: Equivariance under \(h_n,B_n\) carries one chosen
241: free star representative to the whole periodic
242: orbit. The outside source, line and finite-cap
243: maps are unchanged.
244: 
245: In the actual lattice marking, flipping \(C_2\)
246: replaces direction \((1,n-1)\) by \((1,n+1)\);
247: the new fan is \(T_{n+1}\). Flipping \(C_1\)
248: replaces \((1,n)\) by \((1,n-2)\), giving
249: \(T_{n-1}\). These are the literal two diagonal
250: replacements in the periodic squares, with the
251: same period group and positive height.
252: The actual Cox conjugation changes the central
253: coordinate by the right native integer. Hence
254: \[
255:  A_{n+1}-A_n=-nJ,\qquad
256:  A_{n-1}-A_n=(n-1)J.                                \tag{SV.15}
257: \]
258: The two are inverse statements for the same
259: oriented elementary comparison. Their exact
260: telescoping, with the independently computed
261: initial fixed-star value \(A_0\), gives
262: \[
263:                    A_n=A_0-J\,\frac{n(n-1)}2
264:                           \quad\text{in }\mathbb Z/28.
265:                                                         \tag{SV.16}
266: \]
267: The integer \(n(n-1)/2\) is integral for every
268: positive, zero or negative \(n\). At \(n=0\)
269: the two first comparisons agree with K62.
270: This computation covers the displayed vertical
271: line of fans only. It makes no assertion about
272: the arbitrary-fan recurrence quarantined after
273: the scalar determinant obstruction.
274: 
275: 
276: The exact certificate is code/part3/scalar_vertical_fans.py, with its
277: JSON and captured output. It verifies 14 symbolic identities and 425
278: signed instances. The actual maps and relative comparison were independently
279: audited by root and checks before promotion. The scope retains canonical
280: ordinary closing by \(q^e\) times the specified source-independent bounded unit;
281: shorter endpoints with an additional source translation are not included.
